{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AWUqBtwWbnAf6oUT8daPb6","type":"tool_result","content":"862\t=== WRITE C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/objective-coverage.md ===\n863\t# KCNA — Objective Coverage Log\n864\t\n865\tTracks which exam competency each chapter covers, at what depth, and when it was last\n866\treviewed. Seeded at Chapter 1 with the full competency registry so it is useful from\n867\tChapter 2 onward.\n868\t\n869\t**Identifier scheme:** `D<domain>.<competency>` — the Lodestar convention established in\n870\tB1. CNCF publishes four domains and thirteen named competencies with **no numbering and\n871\tno sub-weights**. Every per-chapter weight figure is authored judgment and must be\n872\tdisclosed as such in front matter.\n873\t\n874\t---\n875\t\n876\t## ⚑ Competency count: 13, not 12\n877\t\n878\t`chapter-lineup.md` (B2, ratified) states \"12 competencies\" and \"twelve named\n879\tcompetencies,\" twice. **This is wrong.** The cached CNCF curriculum enumerates\n880\t4 + 4 + 2 + 3 = **13**, and B1's own `D1.1`–`D4.3` scheme yields 13 identifiers.\n881\tChapter 1's domain table is correct.\n882\t\n883\t**Correct B2 before Chapter 19's synthesis, the blueprint appendix, or the front-matter\n884\tdisclosure inherits the wrong figure.** (Author action — outside Stage 14's write scope.)\n885\t\n886\tSources: `lf-kcna-exam-page-2026-08-23`, `cncf-kcna-curriculum-pdf-2026-08-23`.\n887\t\n888\t---\n889\t\n890\t## Coverage by chapter\n891\t\n892\t| Objective | First covered in | Depth | Last reviewed |\n893\t|---|---|---|---|\n894\t| — (none) | Chapter 1 | n/a — orientation chapter, 0% weight, `objectives: []` | 2026-08-24 |\n895\t\n896\tChapter 1 covers no exam objectives. It establishes exam mechanics, the 2025 blueprint\n897\trestructure, and the cloud-native framing that Chapter 17 later harvests. It does\n898\t**name** roughly twenty terms belonging to later competencies without teaching them —\n899\tthose are tracked as reserved entries in `glossary.md`, not as coverage.\n900\t\n901\t---\n902\t\n903\t## Competency registry (13) — planned homes from B2\n904\t\n905\t| ID | Competency | Domain (weight) | Planned chapter(s) | Status |\n906\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n907\t| D1.1 | Kubernetes Core Concepts | Kubernetes Fundamentals (44%) | Ch 3, 4, 5, 6 | not yet covered |\n908\t| D1.2 | Administration | Kubernetes Fundamentals (44%) | Ch 8 | not yet covered |\n909\t| D1.3 | Scheduling | Kubernetes Fundamentals (44%) | Ch 7 | not yet covered |\n910\t| D1.4 | Containerization | Kubernetes Fundamentals (44%) | Ch 2 | not yet covered |\n911\t| D2.1 | Networking | Container Orchestration (28%) | Ch 9, 10 | not yet covered |\n912\t| D2.2 | Security | Container Orchestration (28%) | Ch 12 (+ Ch 10 boundary) | not yet covered |\n913\t| D2.3 | Troubleshooting | Container Orchestration (28%) | Ch 13 | not yet covered |\n914\t| D2.4 | Storage | Container Orchestration (28%) | Ch 11 | not yet covered |\n915\t| D3.1 | Application Delivery | Cloud Native Application Delivery (16%) | Ch 14, 15 | not yet covered |\n916\t| D3.2 | Debugging | Cloud Native Application Delivery (16%) | Ch 16 | not yet covered |\n917\t| D4.1 | Observability | Cloud Native Architecture (12%) | Ch 18 | not yet covered |\n918\t| D4.2 | Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles | Cloud Native Architecture (12%) | Ch 17 | not yet covered |\n919\t| D4.3 | Cloud Native Community and Collaboration | Cloud Native Architecture (12%) | Ch 17 | not yet covered |\n920\t\n921\t**Note on D4.3:** B1 flags it as the competency technically-strong candidates most\n922\treliably under-study. B2's mitigation is not a separate chapter but explicit treatment\n923\tinside Ch 17 — its own numbered sections, Fixed Points, and Soundings coverage — plus\n924\tdisproportionate representation in the Ch 19 synthesis and the Ch 20 mock. Track that\n925\tthis actually happens.\n926\t\n927\t**Curriculum typo worth recording:** the CNCF-published `KCNA_Curriculum.pdf` contains\n928\t\"Could Native Community and Collaboration\" for D4.3. Candidates who download it will see\n929\tit. Belongs in the blueprint appendix.\n930\t=== END WRITE ===\n931\t\n932\t=== WRITE C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/retrieval-log.md ===\n933\t# KCNA — Retrieval-Practice Ledger\n934\t\n935\tTracks which earlier-chapter topics have been retrieval-tested, and in which later\n936\tchapter. Also records forward commitments the prose has made to the reader, which are\n937\tbinding contracts rather than preferences.\n938\t\n939\t---\n940\t\n941\t## Retrieval items by chapter\n942\t\n943\t| Tested topic | Original chapter | Retested in |\n944\t|---|---|---|\n945\t| *(none — Chapter 1 is excluded from the retrieval schedule by design)* | — | — |\n946\t\n947\t**Chapter 1: 0 retrieval items, which is correct.** B3 excludes Ch 1 entirely — the\n948\tskill's table assumes Ch 1 is a content chapter, but here it is orientation at 0%\n949\tweight. The ramp begins at **Ch 3 (10%, drawing from Ch 2)**. The question-quality audit\n950\tconfirmed 0%/0% compliance.\n951\t\n952\t---\n953\t\n954\t## ⚑ Forward commitments — binding\n955\t\n956\t| # | Commitment | Where stated | Status |\n957\t|---|---|---|---|\n958\t| 1 | **Chapter 13's checkpoint must carry a Chapter 8 retrieval item** (version skew, framed as a troubleshooting cause) | Ch 1 §5, in plain reader-facing prose; QC2.2 makes the pairing a whole question | **OPEN — verify at Ch 13 Stage 13** |\n959\t\n960\t**Why #1 is a contract, not a preference.** Chapter 1 tells the reader the pairing by\n961\tname, then builds a checkpoint question around it whose distractor C asserts (correctly,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a2c44320-c026-4b9a-b495-33fa90758087","uuid":"24b8501a-cb25-43a5-ab1e-3e1ee8c88fff","timestamp":"2026-08-24T18:44:13.632Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-01\\kb-manifest.md","content":"=== WRITE C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/objective-coverage.md ===\n# KCNA — Objective Coverage Log\n\nTracks which exam competency each chapter covers, at what depth, and when it was last\nreviewed. Seeded at Chapter 1 with the full competency registry so it is useful from\nChapter 2 onward.\n\n**Identifier scheme:** `D<domain>.<competency>` — the Lodestar convention established in\nB1. CNCF publishes four domains and thirteen named competencies with **no numbering and\nno sub-weights**. Every per-chapter weight figure is authored judgment and must be\ndisclosed as such in front matter.\n\n---\n\n## ⚑ Competency count: 13, not 12\n\n`chapter-lineup.md` (B2, ratified) states \"12 competencies\" and \"twelve named\ncompetencies,\" twice. **This is wrong.** The cached CNCF curriculum enumerates\n4 + 4 + 2 + 3 = **13**, and B1's own `D1.1`–`D4.3` scheme yields 13 identifiers.\nChapter 1's domain table is correct.\n\n**Correct B2 before Chapter 19's synthesis, the blueprint appendix, or the front-matter\ndisclosure inherits the wrong figure.** (Author action — outside Stage 14's write scope.)\n\nSources: `lf-kcna-exam-page-2026-08-23`, `cncf-kcna-curriculum-pdf-2026-08-23`.\n\n---\n\n## Coverage by chapter\n\n| Objective | First covered in | Depth | Last reviewed |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| — (none) | Chapter 1 | n/a — orientation chapter, 0% weight, `objectives: []` | 2026-08-24 |\n\nChapter 1 covers no exam objectives. It establishes exam mechanics, the 2025 blueprint\nrestructure, and the cloud-native framing that Chapter 17 later harvests. It does\n**name** roughly twenty terms belonging to later competencies without teaching them —\nthose are tracked as reserved entries in `glossary.md`, not as coverage.\n\n---\n\n## Competency registry (13) — planned homes from B2\n\n| ID | Competency | Domain (weight) | Planned chapter(s) | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| D1.1 | Kubernetes Core Concepts | Kubernetes Fundamentals (44%) | Ch 3, 4, 5, 6 | not yet covered |\n| D1.2 | Administration | Kubernetes Fundamentals (44%) | Ch 8 | not yet covered |\n| D1.3 | Scheduling | Kubernetes Fundamentals (44%) | Ch 7 | not yet covered |\n| D1.4 | Containerization | Kubernetes Fundamentals (44%) | Ch 2 | not yet covered |\n| D2.1 | Networking | Container Orchestration (28%) | Ch 9, 10 | not yet covered |\n| D2.2 | Security | Container Orchestration (28%) | Ch 12 (+ Ch 10 boundary) | not yet covered |\n| D2.3 | Troubleshooting | Container Orchestration (28%) | Ch 13 | not yet covered |\n| D2.4 | Storage | Container Orchestration (28%) | Ch 11 | not yet covered |\n| D3.1 | Application Delivery | Cloud Native Application Delivery (16%) | Ch 14, 15 | not yet covered |\n| D3.2 | Debugging | Cloud Native Application Delivery (16%) | Ch 16 | not yet covered |\n| D4.1 | Observability | Cloud Native Architecture (12%) | Ch 18 | not yet covered |\n| D4.2 | Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles | Cloud Native Architecture (12%) | Ch 17 | not yet covered |\n| D4.3 | Cloud Native Community and Collaboration | Cloud Native Architecture (12%) | Ch 17 | not yet covered |\n\n**Note on D4.3:** B1 flags it as the competency technically-strong candidates most\nreliably under-study. B2's mitigation is not a separate chapter but explicit treatment\ninside Ch 17 — its own numbered sections, Fixed Points, and Soundings coverage — plus\ndisproportionate representation in the Ch 19 synthesis and the Ch 20 mock. Track that\nthis actually happens.\n\n**Curriculum typo worth recording:** the CNCF-published `KCNA_Curriculum.pdf` contains\n\"Could Native Community and Collaboration\" for D4.3. Candidates who download it will see\nit. Belongs in the blueprint appendix.\n=== END WRITE ===\n\n=== WRITE C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/retrieval-log.md ===\n# KCNA — Retrieval-Practice Ledger\n\nTracks which earlier-chapter topics have been retrieval-tested, and in which later\nchapter. Also records forward commitments the prose has made to the reader, which are\nbinding contracts rather than preferences.\n\n---\n\n## Retrieval items by chapter\n\n| Tested topic | Original chapter | Retested in |\n|---|---|---|\n| *(none — Chapter 1 is excluded from the retrieval schedule by design)* | — | — |\n\n**Chapter 1: 0 retrieval items, which is correct.** B3 excludes Ch 1 entirely — the\nskill's table assumes Ch 1 is a content chapter, but here it is orientation at 0%\nweight. The ramp begins at **Ch 3 (10%, drawing from Ch 2)**. The question-quality audit\nconfirmed 0%/0% compliance.\n\n---\n\n## ⚑ Forward commitments — binding\n\n| # | Commitment | Where stated | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Chapter 13's checkpoint must carry a Chapter 8 retrieval item** (version skew, framed as a troubleshooting cause) | Ch 1 §5, in plain reader-facing prose; QC2.2 makes the pairing a whole question | **OPEN — verify at Ch 13 Stage 13** |\n\n**Why #1 is a contract, not a preference.** Chapter 1 tells the reader the pairing by\nname, then builds a checkpoint question around it whose distractor C asserts (correctly,","numLines":100,"startLine":862,"totalLines":1058}}}
